            <ArticleTitle>Data on HepG2 cells changes following exposure to cadmium sulphide quantum dots (CdS QDs).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>72-97</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.dib.2016.12.051</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The data included in this paper are associated with the research article entitled &quot;Markers for toxicity to HepG2 exposed to cadmium sulphide quantum dots; damage to mitochondria&quot; (Paesano et al.) [1]. The article concerns the cytotoxic and genotoxic effects of CdS QDs in HepG2 cells and the mechanisms involved. In this dataset, changes in expression levels of candidate genes are reported, together with details concerning synthesis and properties of CdS QDs, additional information obtained through literature survey, measures of the mitochondrial membrane potential and the glutathione redox state.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
